---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const schemaNodes = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    '@id': `${site.url}/about/#page`,
    name: 'About OptimisedWebsite',
    description: 'OptimisedWebsite is a specialist studio that builds SEO-first websites for UK businesses. Every site is constructed from keyword research and topical authority architecture.',
    url: `${site.url}/about/`,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${site.url}/#website` },
    mainEntity: { '@id': `${site.url}/#organization` }
  }
];
---
<Base
  title="About OptimisedWebsite | SEO-First Website Studio"
  description="OptimisedWebsite is a specialist studio that builds SEO-first websites for UK businesses. Every site is constructed from keyword research and topical authority architecture."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  schemaNodes={schemaNodes}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'About', href: '/about/' }
    ]} />

    <section class="py-10">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand">About OptimisedWebsite</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        OptimisedWebsite is a specialist studio that builds websites designed to rank. Not redesigns, not template installs, not WordPress themes with a few plugins bolted on. Every site we deliver is constructed from the ground up using keyword research, topical authority architecture, and per-page schema markup.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand mb-4">Why SEO-First Matters</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Most websites are built design-first. A designer creates layouts, a developer codes them, and then someone tries to retrofit SEO — adding meta tags, fixing heading hierarchy, writing alt text. The result is a site that looks polished but lacks the structural foundations search engines need to understand and rank content properly.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        An SEO-first approach reverses that sequence entirely. Before a single line of HTML is written, we complete keyword research, build a topical map, define the internal linking architecture, and plan the schema markup. Every URL, every heading, and every internal link exists because the data justified it. Design serves the structure, not the other way around.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand mb-4">How Topical Authority Works</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Search engines rank websites that demonstrate comprehensive coverage of a subject. A single page targeting "vibration plates" will struggle against a site that covers vibration plate reviews, comparisons, buying guides, exercise routines, health benefits, and brand breakdowns — all interlinked through a hub-and-spoke structure.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Topical authority is not about publishing more pages. It is about publishing the right pages, targeting the right keywords, and connecting them with the right internal links. Our topical maps typically contain 15-50 pages organised into 3-7 clusters, each covering a subtopic within your niche at sufficient depth that search engines treat your site as the go-to resource.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand mb-4">What Makes Our Builds Different</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Three things separate our builds from a typical web agency deliverable. First, every page carries its own JSON-LD schema block within a site-wide @graph — Organisation, WebSite, Service, Article, FAQPage, HowTo, and BreadcrumbList types are deployed where the data supports them, cross-referenced through @id for entity coherence.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Second, we build on Astro and deploy to CDN edge networks (Cloudflare Pages or Vercel). The result is static HTML with zero server-side rendering overhead, sub-second page loads, and Core Web Vitals scores that put you ahead of WordPress competitors still loading jQuery and twelve plugins.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Third, you own everything. The GitHub repository, the domain, the hosting account, and the content. There is no proprietary CMS, no vendor lock-in, and no recurring platform fee. If you want to walk away and manage the site yourself, you can — we hand over a complete codebase with documentation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-10 text-center">
      <CTA href="/portfolio/" label="View Our Portfolio" />
      <span class="inline-block mx-2"></span>
      <CTA href="/order/" label="Order a Build" variant="secondary" />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
